08"] "\n" [:option {:value "35511"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "35519"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "35542"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "35547"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "35613"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "35641"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "35685"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "35743"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "35806"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "35882"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "35957"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "36002"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "36041"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "36108"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "36185"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "36262"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "36346"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "36438"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "260100"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "315000"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "358460"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19001350"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2002620"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/337"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Hockey, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "31 July – 13 August 1948"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/339"} "Empire Stadium, Wembley, London"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/358"} "John Lyons' Sports Ground, Sudbury Hill, London"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/359"} "Polytechnic Sports Ground, Chiswick, London"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/360"} "Guinness Sports Ground, Park Royal, London"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/35579"} "187 from 13 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Round-robin pools advance teams to classification round matches."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In five Olympic hockey tournaments, there had only been two different winners, but Great Britain and India had never competed together at the Olympics. In fact, the two nations had never played each other, the British fearing embarrassment as their (former) colony was considered the better team. There was no question the UK would again be absent at their home Olympics, although there were some organizational difficulties. First of all, the four British nations were independently affiliated with the " [:a {:href "/organizations/65"} "FIH"] " international federation and weren’t very keen on cooperating. Also, there were no hockey grounds to train on, as these were used by cricketers during the summer. Still, they managed to put together a team, the first real British hockey team at the Olympics (the " [:a {:href "/results/35500"} "1908"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/35511"} "1920"] " champions had been composed entirely of English players). Their captain was the versatile " [:a {:href "/athletes/18721"} "Norman Borrett"] ", a first class cricketer and national squash champion who once qualified for Wimbledon but didn’t have time to compete."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Britain and India were seeded, along with Pakistan and the Netherlands. Pakistan had only separated from India the previous year, and made their first Olympic appearance in London. One of the team members, " [:a {:href "/athletes/19163"} "Ali Dara"] ", had been on the golden Indian team of " [:a {:href "/results/35547"} "1936"] ". All four ranked teams made the semis, although the Brits were held to a goalless draw by Switzerland, and Pakistan crushed the Dutch 6-1 in their group match."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The semi-finals were close, and British observers considered the Indians to be lucky to get away with a 2-1 win against the Dutch. With Britain beating Pakistan, the gold medal match would finally see India play the Britons. Completely focused on its defense, Britain was unable to keep up with the fast-paced Indians, and they lost it 4-0. The bronze went to the Netherlands, beating Pakistan 4-1 in a replay of the first 3rd place match, which had ended in a draw."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button746299", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button746299').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-512303"} [:div {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-plus"}]] [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "India"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IND"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IND.png"}] "IND"]] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-512303 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/19178"} "Ranganathan Francis"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "2"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "0"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-512303 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/19300"} "Tarlochan Singh Bawa"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "5"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "2"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-512303 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/19966"} "Akhtar Hussain"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "1"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "0"] [:t